  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts and it passes the typecheck tool. I couldn't run `vite build` or open the page, so I haven't seen a rendered frame.\n\n- **Instancing:** the scene has a ground plane and four instanced nodes. These are 8,000 trunks (cylinders), 8,000 canopies (cones) and 2,000 rocks (squashed spheres), drawn as 3 instanced calls, not 10,000 meshes. Positions are scattered over a radius-60 disc from a seeded linear congruential generator (LCG) with seed 20240607, so the forest is the same on every load.\n- **Colour:** each canopy and each rock gets its own HSL colour (greens for canopies, greys and browns for rocks). Trunks share one brown material.\n- **Light and fog:** there is one directional \"sun\" with `shadow: true`, plus a hemisphere light for fill. Fog is `effects.fog` with `mode: \"exp\"` (exponential), density 0.003.\n- **Camera:** an `onFrame` callback moves the camera with `app.camera?.setPose` in a circle of radius 105 at height 62. It turns at 0.1 rad/s, about one lap per minute, and always looks at the origin. By my estimate, at that distance and a 45° field of view the whole forest fits in the 640x360 frame.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set to true one animation frame after the first `onFrame` callback.\n\n",
